reconstructd protocol: TCP port 7077, JSON Lines, one response per request.
Requests and replies are JSON objects. Successful replies contain ok:true; errors contain ok:false and error.
begin is {op,run_id,channels,calibration,modes}. frame is {op,run_id,seq,data}, where data is base64 of channels signed little-endian int16 values followed by a little-endian CRC-16/CCITT over the value bytes, polynomial 0x1021 and initial 0xffff. correction is {op,run_id,seq,corrections}; corrections are additive raw ADC values. finalize and query are {op,run_id}.
The order is begin, frame/correction, finalize, query. Invalid order does not mutate state. Bad frame data returns BAD_FRAME and increments rejected. Valid duplicate sequences replace the previous frame and increment duplicate. Frames are sorted by sequence; integer gaps between minimum and maximum are missing observations.
The decoder executable is /usr/local/libexec/modalcodec. Its binary input is uint32 little-endian calibration, uint16 little-endian channels, uint16 little-endian modes, then corrected calibrated int16 channels. Its output is little-endian float64 modal coefficients. Revision 1 uses gain 1 offset 0; revision 2 uses gain 1.25 offset -3; revision 3 uses gain .75 offset 4. Coefficient j is sum over i of ((((i+1)*(j+2)) mod 17)-8)*calibrated[i]/9 plus (j+1)*.125.
Reports contain run_id, calibration, counts with accepted/rejected/duplicate/missing, mean, covariance, eigenvalues, and eigenvectors. Eigenvalues descend and eigenvectors are normalized columns with their largest-magnitude component positive. Missing observations are excluded from statistics. Numeric values are JSON doubles.
